# The weapon in the glove on the classic arm (#385.10, #466.2): with `arms classic-hand glove` the Arx hand is hidden
# and the glove drawn at its wrist; the held sword keeps the Arx hand's placement (#75, D-033: the hilt on the hidden
# hand's palm attach point, the blade along the controller's handle) - held ahead, raised to the face and with the hand
# 1.5 m out past the reach. The placement from the glove's own hilt frame went with the custom, forearm and hands models
# (#486); `grip tilt` still stores and snaps cfg.ini vr_sword_tilt (vr.weapon.tilt), which nothing applies until #548.
# The right hand holds the sword (mvp-items). The pose numbers are a first guess: move the POSE, never the assertions.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 weapon-in-glove
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence weapon-in-glove -Save mvp-items
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
arms classic
arms classic-hand glove
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.active eq true
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq classic
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.right.custom.gloveDrawn eq true
@assert vr.body.right.classic.arxHandHidden eq true
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true

# 1. The sword in the glove keeps the Arx hand's placement: on the hidden hand's palm, the blade along the handle
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt 2
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToPalm lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq 0
@shot glove-default

# 2. The same raised to the face, the hand turned
vr-sim hand right pos 0.12 -0.1 -0.35
vr-sim hand right rot 0 90 0
vr-sim head rot 0 -15 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt 2
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToPalm lt 0.5
@shot glove-raised

# 3. A hand past the reach: the weapon stays in the hand with the glove
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
vr-sim hand left off
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -1.5
vr-sim hand right rot 0 0 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.right.custom.gloveDrawn eq true
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt 2
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToPalm lt 0.5
@shot glove-far
vr-sim hand left on
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -0.35
@frames 20

# 4. The tilt switch: the status follows; a value off the table is refused or snapped to a variant - never stored as is
grip tilt -15
@frames 5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq -15
grip tilt 40
@frames 5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt le 0
@assert vr.weapon.tilt ge -30
grip tilt 0
@frames 5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq 0

# 5. Back to the Arx hand: the same placement
arms classic-hand arx
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.right.custom.gloveDrawn eq false
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt 2
@shot arx-hand

@assert errors eq 0
